# Dropdowns and source tools use the same bounded choice surface.
import choice_popovers.dl

to get [the UI popup font in] {a pointer to UI view:view}:
    if view's instance's description's kind = 40:
        return view's popup's typeface
    return view's small

to get [the UI popup appearance in] {a pointer to UI view:view}:
    if view's instance's description's kind = 40:
        return view's popup's appearance
    set result to default UI appearance settings
    set result's background to view's theme's surface
    set result's foreground to view's theme's text
    return result

to [refresh UI popup choices in] {a pointer to UI view:view}:
    set owner to view's popup
    set popup to the address of (view's popup choices)
    set item to popup's first item
    set child to owner's first
    loop while child != @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI layout):
        set item's label to (the UI value for (child's node) in (view's instance))'s text
        set item's enabled to the UI element (child's node) is enabled in (view's instance)
        set item's icon to child's node's variant
        if owner's node's kind = 34:
            if ((the UI value for (owner's node) in (view's instance))'s text) = item's label:
                set item's icon to "check"
        set child to child's next
        set item to item's next
    if popup's selected >= 0:
        if (the UI choice at (popup's selected) in popup)'s enabled = false:
            move UI choice selection in popup by 1 wrapping true
    set typeface to the UI popup font in view
    set width to the maximum of 196.0 and (owner's painted bounds' width)
    set item to popup's first item
    loop while item != @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI choice):
        set width to the maximum of width and ((the width of (item's label) using typeface) + 64.0)
        set item to item's next
    set popup's preferred width to width
    set anchor to owner's painted bounds
    place UI choice popover popup anchored at anchor within (the UI viewport bounds in view) using typeface

to [open UI popup for] {a pointer to UI layout:layout} [in] {a pointer to UI view:view}:
    set popup to the address of (view's popup choices)
    clear UI choice popover popup in view
    set view's popup to layout
    set popup's on release to true
    set popup's accepts space to true
    set child to layout's first
    loop while child != @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI layout):
        add UI choice ((the UI value for (child's node) in (view's instance))'s text) enabled (the UI element (child's node) is enabled in (view's instance)) to popup
        set child to child's next
    if layout's node's kind = 34:
        set popup's selected to (the UI value for (layout's node) in (view's instance))'s number
    show UI choice popover popup reporting "" with hint "" in view
    refresh UI popup choices in view
